Figure~\ref{fig:parabola} shows a parabola. The code is

\begin{verbatim}
for n in range(10):
    print(n, r(n))   # 100% plain
\end{verbatim}

and, as Hardy wrote,

\begin{quote}
A mathematician, like a painter or a poet, is a maker of patterns.

\end{quote}

\begin{corollary}\label{cor:gaps}
$g(x) \ll x^{1/4} \log x$.

\end{corollary}

\appendix

\section{A computation}\label{app:comp}

\begin{lemma}\label{lem:numerics}
For $x \leq 10^{12}$ we have $g(x) \leq 2 x^{1/4}$; Erdős and Turán knew this, see Appendix~\ref{app:comp}.

\end{lemma}

